                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… зазнава́ться"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                        "entry_id": "aa427365-88e0-35d3-a66a-f8b61b465a72",
                        "glosses": [
                            "вести себя высокомерно, надменно; важничать, пренебрежительно относиться к другим"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3460729c-2ab2-4df3-ac10-f3306d0081ef",
                                "sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                                "text": "Осип Иванович и в княжеском доме не зазнавался: был по-прежнему тих и смирен, изредка только опаздывал к делу, зазевавшись, по всегдашней привычке своей, на улице."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b85b01c4-de70-426f-9646-5c4e068b5c42",
                                "sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                                "text": "Баловень родных, друзей и прекрасного пола, при постоянных успехах и среди многих заблуждений своей счастливой молодости он никогда не зазнавался, всегда оставался доброжелателен, сострадателен и любящ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b7d9663-76ad-42a4-8869-d45f7da02be4",
                                "sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                                "text": "А тот, кто зазнаётся, кто влюбляется в самого себя, кто забывает о других ради своего честолюбия, ― тот неизбежно оказывается изолированным, одиноким и ― хуже того ― отсталым человеком."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02478159-f902-4d9a-b0cf-43de69204e1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa427365-88e0-35d3-a66a-f8b61b465a72",
                        "source_sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                        "target_lang_word": "give oneself airs",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "give oneself airs",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbc59201-974e-38e0-9202-4e5f6ad67013",
                                        "entry_id": "86d3c58f-6af1-330f-8e54-7e110d88be44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act pretentiously, or in a snobbish manner; to swagger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c6c4d8a-f6f0-4af6-855a-04f8087ee2f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa427365-88e0-35d3-a66a-f8b61b465a72",
                        "source_sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
                        "target_lang_word": "put on frills",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "put on frills",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c682da5-30a9-3dbe-9735-64afe167c27c",
                                        "entry_id": "ce5c9122-3a8a-3db8-9364-750ef63ae62f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act in a pretentious or snobbish way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99788e10-0577-4fad-9bcf-be75098b24f4",
                                                "sense_id": "4c682da5-30a9-3dbe-9735-64afe167c27c",
                                                "text": "[…] he put his head in again, and cussed me for putting on frills and trying to be better than him; and when I reckoned he was gone, he come back and put his head in again, and told me to mind about that school, because he was going to lay for me and lick me if I didn’t drop that."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e957d9e-ca79-4d98-902b-dca2ec86a7d8",
                                                "sense_id": "4c682da5-30a9-3dbe-9735-64afe167c27c",
                                                "text": "“She said we were really the only people on the ship they cared to know.”\n“I shouldn’t have thought a missionary was such a big bug that he could afford to put on frills.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5f613a0-06b3-4bc3-b93e-e72525773b03",
                                                "sense_id": "4c682da5-30a9-3dbe-9735-64afe167c27c",
                                                "text": "[…] your sneers against Doctor Hardy are lies! He doesn’t put on frills, or have an office in a fashionable location, or drive around in an expensive automobile."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1419b6b3-d44a-4123-af6b-0a06e5927464",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa427365-88e0-35d3-a66a-f8b61b465a72",
                        "source_sense_id": "64cc390d-c44d-3812-93eb-270917d22dcb",
